rh56dftp_description
====================

This package adapts and builds upon third-party open-source work. Attribution
below is required by the respective licenses and by project policy.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. rh56dfx_description  (URDF/xacro, meshes, joint config — reused/adapted)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Source : https://github.com/ookkshirsagar/rh56dfx_description
   Author : Omkar Chandrakant Kshirsagar (Fraunhofer IPA)
   License: MIT (see ./LICENSE)

   Reused VERBATIM:
     - meshes/left/**, meshes/right/**            (all visual + collision STL)
   Reused with MODIFICATION:
     - urdf/rh56dftp_macro.xacro   (from urdf/rh56dfx_macro.xacro):
         renamed macro rh56dfx_hand -> rh56dftp_hand and the mesh package path
         rh56dfx_description -> rh56dftp_description; normalized CRLF->LF;
         removed one stray 'ac' token (source typo). Kinematics — joints, limits,
         mimic tags, inertials — are UNCHANGED.
     - urdf/rh56dftp.xacro         (from urdf/rh56dfx.xacro): renamed, fixed the
         world-link child reference, default prefix set to "<side>_".
   NOT reused:
     - the ROS2 ament packaging (package.xml, CMakeLists.txt, launch/, rviz/,
       config/ros2_controllers.yaml, MoveIt joint_limits/joint_names.yaml). This
       package is deliberately framework-agnostic (no ROS dependency).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. inspire-hand-rh56-py  (tactile protocol reference)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Source : https://github.com/yuzhench/inspire-hand-rh56-py
   Used as a REFERENCE ONLY for the RH56DFTP tactile (Modbus) protocol. No code
   was copied. The tactile region map in tactile/tactile_layout.yaml is derived
   from the DDS driver shipped in this workspace
   (inspire_hand_sdk/inspire_sdkpy/inspire_hand_defaut.py :: data_sheet), which
   is the live source of truth for the sensor register layout.

